re and one of 3 metres.  Each competitor made seven dives, four compulsory and three optional.  Two compulsory dives were made from the 1-metre springboard, a plain running dive and a running forward somersault; and two were made from the 3-metre springboard, a 1 somersault and a backward spring with forward dive.  The optional dives were made from the 3-metre springboard."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Germany dominated this event.  In the first round, the top score was posted by " [:a {:href "/athletes/47778"} "Kurt Behrens"] ", while in the semi-finals he was second to the United States’ " [:a {:href "/athletes/51350"} "George Gaidzik"] ".  The winner in the finals, however, was the 18-year-old " [:a {:href "/athletes/47959"} "Albert Zürner"] ", who narrowly defeated Behrens, and whose main claim to fame was having been Champion of Hamburg (Germany) for the past four years.  Tying for third with Gaidzik was " [:a {:href "/athletes/47941"} "Gottlob Walz"] ", who was the heavy favorite.  Walz had won the platform competition at the " [:a {:href "/results/54001"} "1906 Olympic Games"] ", was an 11-time German champion, and had won the European championship three times (first in 1903)."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/47959"} "Albert Zürner"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} "83.60 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "82.80 (2 h2)"] [:td {} "85.50 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/47778"} "Kurt Behrens"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https:/